 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Washington has a new idea for Ukraine: stop striking each other's power grids. Moscow has already pushed back."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "On Friday and Saturday, U.S. envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner hosted talks in Miami with Ukrainian and European officials. According to Axios, the plan is a partial ceasefire covering energy infrastructure and grain shipments."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "The talks follow one of Russia's biggest strikes of the war. On October seventh, Ukraine says Russia fired about seventy missiles and one hundred thirty drones across twelve regions. Reports put the death toll at twenty or more. Zelenskyy said energy sites were a key target."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Ukraine says it is open to an energy ceasefire. The Kremlin says it wants a comprehensive settlement, not temporary ceasefires. Spokesman Dmitry Peskov also sees no near-term summit with Trump, Zelenskyy and Putin. No deal has been announced. Winter is close."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Follow for the next update."
  }
 ],
